 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "The pirates are getting closer,",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 1.589
  },
  {
   "text": "and the ship's cook is pouring oil into the sea.",
   "s": 1.78,
   "e": 4.176
  },
  {
   "text": "The captain grabs him by the apron.",
   "s": 4.669,
   "e": 6.35
  },
  {
   "text": "They're about to board us, and you're cooking?",
   "s": 6.798,
   "e": 8.865
  },
  {
   "text": "He doesn't look up.",
   "s": 9.433,
   "e": 10.117
  },
  {
   "text": "He just points.",
   "s": 10.668,
   "e": 11.493
  },
  {
   "text": "Black clouds.",
   "s": 11.97,
   "e": 12.953
  },
  {
   "text": "A storm.",
   "s": 13.281,
   "e": 13.963
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody survives a storm like that.",
   "s": 14.275,
   "e": 16.137
  },
  {
   "text": "Trust the oil,",
   "s": 16.666,
   "e": 17.622
  },
  {
   "text": "says the cook.",
   "s": 17.865,
   "e": 18.483
  },
  {
   "text": "A grappling hook bangs off the rail.",
   "s": 19.013,
   "e": 20.892
  },
  {
   "text": "The captain spins the wheel.",
   "s": 21.232,
   "e": 22.655
  },
  {
   "text": "And the pirates?",
   "s": 23.152,
   "e": 23.893
  },
  {
   "text": "They're thrilled.",
   "s": 24.198,
   "e": 25.085
  },
  {
   "text": "Why waste cannonballs, when the storm will sink them for free?",
   "s": 25.436,
   "e": 28.345
  },
  {
   "text": "The waves grow taller than the mast.",
   "s": 28.887,
   "e": 30.866
  },
  {
   "text": "The crew ties themselves to anything nailed down.",
   "s": 31.195,
   "e": 33.706
  },
  {
   "text": "But the cook keeps pouring.",
   "s": 34.186,
   "e": 35.608
  },
  {
   "text": "Always on the windy side.",
   "s": 36.038,
   "e": 37.492
  },
  {
   "text": "The pirates swing in to board.",
   "s": 37.998,
   "e": 39.581
  },
  {
   "text": "And straight ahead,",
   "s": 39.944,
   "e": 40.86
  },
  {
   "text": "a wave big enough to swallow both ships rises out of the dark.",
   "s": 41.081,
   "e": 44.675
  },
  {
   "text": "You see,",
   "s": 45.17,
   "e": 45.58
  },
  {
   "text": "sailors really did carry oil for this.",
   "s": 45.796,
   "e": 47.949
  },
  {
   "text": "They called it storm oil.",
   "s": 48.331,
   "e": 49.597
  },
  {
   "text": "Blow on soup.",
   "s": 50.236,
   "e": 51.139
  },
  {
   "text": "The broth ripples,",
   "s": 51.714,
   "e": 52.798
  },
  {
   "text": "but the oily spots stay flat.",
   "s": 52.934,
   "e": 54.516
  },
  {
   "text": "Your breath can't grip them.",
   "s": 54.974,
   "e": 56.237
  },
  {
   "text": "Same with the sea.",
   "s": 56.687,
   "e": 57.421
  },
  {
   "text": "No grip,",
   "s": 57.8,
   "e": 58.226
  },
  {
   "text": "no breaking wave.",
   "s": 58.612,
   "e": 59.544
  },
  {
   "text": "So when the wave hits their oily patch, it just lifts the ship,",
   "s": 59.971,
   "e": 62.989
  },
  {
   "text": "and puts it back down.",
   "s": 63.243,
   "e": 64.21
  },
  {
   "text": "Fifty yards behind,",
   "s": 64.617,
   "e": 65.741
  },
  {
   "text": "it curls over, and crashes right onto the pirates' deck.",
   "s": 65.887,
   "e": 69.044
  }
 ]
